# Titanic Survival Prediction Using K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)

## Project Overview

This project implements a supervised machine learning model to predict Titanic passenger survival using the **K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)** classification algorithm. Developed in Python, it demonstrates an end-to-end machine learning workflow involving data exploration, missing-value handling, feature engineering, hyperparameter tuning, model evaluation, and visualization.

The model uses Scikit-learn pipelines and GridSearchCV to identify suitable KNN parameters and evaluates its predictions using accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and a confusion matrix.

## Project Objectives

- Explore and understand the Titanic passenger dataset.
- Identify and handle missing values.
- Engineer features that describe passenger and family characteristics.
- Train a KNN classification model.
- Optimize model parameters using five-fold cross-validation.
- Evaluate classification performance on a held-out test set.
- Visualize actual versus predicted survival outcomes.

