## How to Run the Project

### 1. Clone the repository

Replace `REPOSITORY-NAME` with the actual repository name.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/KE2541/REPOSITORY-NAME.git
cd REPOSITORY-NAME
```

### 2. Create and activate a virtual environment (optional)

On Windows PowerShell:

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

### 3. Install dependencies

```bash
python -m pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn
```

### 4. Add the dataset

Place `tested.csv` in the same directory as `scikit.py`.

### 5. Run the script

```bash
python scikit.py
```

The script displays dataset information, missing-value counts, preprocessed data, optimal hyperparameters, cross-validation accuracy, test metrics, the confusion matrix, and the confusion matrix heatmap.

